ype {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f7ec07d-8c52-59b5-bf08-7e8ede02b4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381609} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc7fa4b3-d671-55a5-b19c-1105182de6e9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22aac00f-b3c2-59cf-a645-08ce6fac9605" :question/math-academy-id "q-182397" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬(P∧¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add a column for $¬Q,$ where the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the column for $Q.$ \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $P∧¬Q.$ Remember that $P∧¬Q$ is true if both $P$ and $¬Q$ are true. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P∧¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $¬(P∧¬Q).$ Remember that the truth values of $¬(P∧¬Q)$ are opposite those of $P∧¬Q.$ \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P∧¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬(P∧¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"}]}
